  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 135 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery reveals a mid-level low spinning near the\nMinnesota/Iowa border with ridging over the Four Corners area.\nSfc analysis indicates the sfc low spinning in central Iowa \nnear Iowa Falls. The OAX CWA is mostly obscured by wrap-around \novercast skies at about 2,000 feet. A few radar returns over \nwestern Iowa are producing sprinkles at best with iso PoPs \ncontinuing on the far eastern edges of the CWA through about 7pm\nthis evening.\n\nThe primary concern is the low's affect on our winds, currently\ngusting 20-30 knots. Those winds are expected to peak around 35\nknots this afternoon and near wind advisory criteria. Have \nopted to forgo issuing one, but it is close. Should they \noverperform, one might need to be issued later this afternoon. \n\nHumidity has slipped. Dewpoints are down a couple of degrees\nfrom yesterday and are expected to drop by a bigger margin for \nSaturday. The NBM's numbers were too high and I took care of\nthat. I've also increased cloud cover a bit due to the impact \nof the elevated wildfire smoke drifting in from the north. That \nsmoke is forecast to peak over the area around 4am Sunday \nmorning at 40-60 mg/m2. I added a 25% minimum for cloud cover \nlate tonight into Sunday and if anything, that's \nunderestimating how much sunshine the smoke will be blocking.",
